  "description": "The White-tailed Kite is a pale raptor of grasslands and open landscapes, with white underparts and tail, gray upperparts, and distinctive black shoulder patches. Its characteristic hunting technique is to hover into the wind, looking down for small mammals moving below. This suspended flight can make the bird seem almost stationary above a field. In the United States, California is one of its principal strongholds. Outside the breeding season, kites may gather to roost together in trees or tall shrubs near their hunting grounds.",
